<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Required for Live Activity PUSH updates.

	  ActivityKit will hand out an activity push token only if the app carries
	  the push entitlement. Without this the activity still starts and still
	  updates while the app is in the foreground, so everything looks fine on
	  the bench - and then the card freezes the moment iOS suspends the app,
	  because the worker never had a token to push to. There is no error
	  anywhere in that story.

	  'development' is correct for builds run from Xcode and for a device
	  provisioned for development, and it pairs with Apns__UseSandbox=true on
	  the worker. TestFlight and the App Store need 'production' against the
	  production APNs host; a token from one environment is rejected outright by
	  the other, as a silent non-delivery.
	-->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
</dict>
</plist>
